@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] galileo-secret-custody
Injected credential values exist only inside per-request authorization
responses. They MUST NOT be persisted, logged, cached or exposed on any
status surface. Guests can use integrations but never read their secrets.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] galileo-authority-boundary
Galileo MUST obtain current Marshall authorization before every upstream
effect and retain it through a bounded renewable lease while that effect is
open. Failed, invalid or late renewal MUST close the existing attempt without
retrying it. Guest headers cannot confer VM identity. Galileo MUST NOT access
Marshall's database.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] galileo-closed-routing
Guest input selects only the integration name, method and path. The target
origin, strip prefix, injected headers and peer endpoints come exclusively
from the closed Marshall authorization response validated by the shared
protocol library.
